>>
Rule 1 (same-rank input tensors must have compatible shapes for broadcasting)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ndim(v_1) > 0 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i) ∨ shape(v_1, i) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, i) = 1
>>
Rule 2 (input tensors have identical rank, shape, and data type)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 1 ∧ ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ dtype_(v_1) = dtype_(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)
>>
Rule 3 (trailing dimension broadcast compatibility between input tensors)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) > 0 ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 then shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1) = shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) - 1) ∨ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) - 1) = 1
>>
Rule 4 (both input tensors must have numeric or boolean data types)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= 0 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 10 ∧ 0 ≤ dtype_(v_2) ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≤ 10
>>
Rule 5 (broadcasting compatibility when comparing a 2D tensor with a 1D tensor)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 2 ∧ ndim(v_2) = 1 then shape(v_2, 0) = shape(v_1, 1) ∨ shape(v_2, 0) = 1 ∨ shape(v_1, 1) = 1
>>
Rule 6 (1-dimensional tensors must have broadcast-compatible shapes)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 1 ∧ ndim(v_2) = 1 then shape(v_1, 0) = shape(v_2, 0) ∨ shape(v_1, 0) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, 0) = 1
>>
Rule 7 (2-dimensional tensors must have broadcast-compatible dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 2 ∧ ndim(v_2) = 2 then (shape(v_1, 0) = shape(v_2, 0) ∨ shape(v_1, 0) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, 0) = 1) ∧ (shape(v_1, 1) = shape(v_2, 1) ∨ shape(v_1, 1) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, 1) = 1)
>>
Rule 8 (data type compatibility between input tensors: boolean with boolean, numeric with numeric)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 0 then dtype_(v_2) = 0 else if 1 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 10 then 1 ≤ dtype_(v_2) ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≤ 10 else false
